  "notes": "Composed of {継|けい} (succeed, inherit) and {続|ぞく} (continue). More formal than {続|つづ}ける and often used in written language, business, and official contexts. The proverb {継続|けいぞく}は{力|ちから}なり ('persistence is power') is one of the most commonly cited Japanese proverbs.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {努力|どりょく}を{継続|けいぞく}する: to continue one's efforts\n- {治療|ちりょう}を{継続|けいぞく}する: to continue treatment\n- {契約|けいやく}を{継続|けいぞく}する: to continue a contract\n- {継続|けいぞく}{的|てき}な: continuous, ongoing\n- {継続|けいぞく}は{力|ちから}なり: persistence is power (proverb)\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- {続|つづ}ける: to continue — everyday verb; more casual and versatile\n- {持続|じぞく}する: to sustain, maintain — emphasizes maintaining something at a consistent level\n- {存続|そんぞく}する: to survive, continue to exist — focuses on the continued existence of an organization or system",
